    "groundContactBasis": "The museum and archaeology literature confirm the palisade trench, possible guardhouse, stone foundations for metallurgical work and 1658 timber-lined well. The McGill catalogue’s written description of Bourdon’s early manuscript lists the chapel and magazine. Morin’s later drawing provides general placement and roof cues, with the excavated timber enclosure taking precedence. Heights and complete building placement are estimates.",
